  note5: 'xmax also records row locks, and a version carrying an xmax is still visible when that transaction aborted. The real rule combines xmin, xmax, and the commit status recorded in pg_xact.',

  s6Number: '06 / THE EXCEPTION: HOT', s6Title: ['Not every UPDATE', 'touches the indexes.'],
  s6Intro: 'The short version — “an UPDATE forces every index to be updated” — is the one most worth correcting. When no indexed column changes and the new version fits on the same page, Postgres writes a heap-only tuple: it chains the old pointer to the new one and the indexes stay untouched.',
  hotSides: [
    ['ORDINARY UPDATE', 'A new index entry', 'If an indexed column changed, or the page has no room, the new address must be written into every affected index.'],
    ['HOT UPDATE', 'A redirect inside the page', 'The old pointer redirects to the new one and the index keeps pointing at the same ctid. Pruning can also reclaim that space without waiting for a full vacuum.'],
  ],
  hotRows: [
    [['INDEX', 'key 100 → (0,2)'], ['(0,1)', 'old version'], ['(0,2)', 'new version']],
    [['INDEX', 'key 100 → (0,1)'], ['(0,1)', 'redirect → lp 3'], ['(0,3)', 'new version']],
  ],
  hotFootLabel: 'CONDITIONS',
  hotFoot: 'No indexed column modified, plus free space on the same page. fillfactor reserves that space; indexing columns that change often disables the HOT path in practice.',

  s7Number: '07 / DEAD TUPLES, BLOAT, VACUUM', s7Title: ['Nothing can be cleaned', 'while someone might read it.'],
  s7Intro: 'An old version is dead only when no running transaction — and none that could start — can need it. That boundary is the horizon, and the oldest transaction still open sets it.',
  horizonCaption: ['TRANSACTION TIMELINE', 'THE OLDEST ONE SETS THE HORIZON'],
  horizonRows: [
    ['T1 · REPORT', 'BEGIN three hours ago · still open'],
    ['T2 · UPDATE', 'commit'],
    ['T3 · UPDATE', 'commit'],
    ['DEAD TUPLES', 'not reclaimable while T1 lives'],
  ],
  horizonFootLabel: 'THE EFFECT',
  horizonFoot: 'While T1 stays open, autovacuum can run, find the old versions, and be unable to remove them. The table and its indexes grow, scans read more pages, and latency rises without a single query having changed.',
  vacuumCards: [
    ['01', 'Dead tuple', 'A version no longer visible to any possible transaction; its space can be recycled.'],
    ['02', 'Horizon', 'Set by the oldest open transaction. Replication slots and standbys with hot_standby_feedback hold it back too.'],
    ['03', 'autovacuum', 'Runs on per-table thresholds; heavily written tables rarely do well on the global defaults.'],
    ['04', 'VACUUM and VACUUM FULL', 'VACUUM recycles space inside pages; VACUUM FULL rewrites the table, returns space to the system, and takes an exclusive lock.'],
    ['05', 'Visibility map', 'Marks all-visible pages: it enables index-only scans and saves work for the next vacuum.'],
    ['06', 'Freeze', 'Vacuum also freezes old tuples to prevent wraparound of the 32-bit transaction counter.'],
  ],
  warningLabel: 'OPERATIONAL SYMPTOM',
  warning: 'A connection sitting idle in transaction for hours is one of the cheapest ways to degrade a healthy database: it burns no CPU, never shows up among slow queries, and still blocks the recycling of a single old version across the whole instance.',

  s8Number: '08 / WHAT TO DO WITH THIS', s8Title: ['From a mental model', 'to operational decisions.'],
  s8Intro: 'Understanding pages, tuples, and MVCC pays off when it changes what you do in design and in daily operations.',
  method: [
    ['01', 'Keep transactions short', 'Open, do the work, close. Never wait on human input or a network call with a BEGIN held open.'],
    ['02', 'Watch the pending work', 'n_dead_tup in pg_stat_user_tables and the age of the oldest transaction in pg_stat_activity explain most bloat incidents.'],
    ['03', 'Tune autovacuum per table', 'Hot tables are rarely served well by the global default thresholds.'],
    ['04', 'Reserve room where updates happen', 'Lowering fillfactor on heavily updated tables makes the HOT path more likely.'],
    ['05', 'Index deliberately', 'Every index on a frequently updated column cancels HOT and adds writes.'],
    ['06', 'Never treat ctid as an identifier', 'It is a physical address: it changes on updates, VACUUM FULL, and CLUSTER.'],
  ],
  vacuumTitle: 'Six terms that show up in every incident',
  checklistKicker: 'DATABASE REVIEW',
  checklistTitle: 'Questions for a database review',
  checklist: [
    'What is the oldest open transaction right now?',
    'How many dead tuples do the most written tables hold?',
    'Does autovacuum keep up, or fall behind during peaks?',
    'Which indexes sit on frequently updated columns?',
    'Are inactive replication slots holding the horizon back?',
    'Did size on disk grow while the row count did not?',
    'Does any part of the code store or compare a ctid?',
  ],
  conclusionKicker: 'THE MODEL IN ONE LINE', conclusionA: 'Page, pointer, version.', conclusionB: 'Everything else follows.',
  conclusionCopy: 'The ctid, indexes pointing into the heap, two connections seeing different prices, bloat, and vacuum are not separate topics: they are one design decision seen from different angles. Postgres would rather write a new version than overwrite the previous one, and its entire operational model follows from that.',
  sourceNumber: '09 / SOURCES', sourceTitle: ['Keep going', 'deeper.'],
  sourceDescriptions: [
    'The video that sparked this note · Hussein Nasser',
    'Header, line pointers, and physical layout',
    'Updates that leave the indexes alone',
    'Snapshots, xmin, xmax, and concurrency control',
    'Read Committed, Repeatable Read, and Serializable',
    'Dead tuples, horizon, freeze, and wraparound',
    'ctid, xmin, xmax, and the other system columns',
  ],
  footer: 'POSTGRES · FIELD NOTE 03', top: 'BACK TO TOP ↑',
};

/* Language-neutral fragments: SQL, chips, and the geometry of the timeline. */
const queries = [
  "SELECT pg_relation_filepath('items');",
  'SHOW block_size;',
  'SELECT ctid, xmin, xmax, price FROM items;',
  "SELECT n_live_tup, n_dead_tup FROM pg_stat_user_tables WHERE relname = 'items';",
];

const pointers = ['lp 1 → 7104', 'lp 2 → 6848', 'lp 3 → free'];

const lookupHits = [2, 1, 2];
const lookupNodes = [
  ['root · 50 | 150', 'branch · 80 | 100', 'leaf · 100 → (0,2)'],
  ['key · 100', 'ctid · (0,2)', 'no row data'],
  ['page 0 · lp 1', 'page 0 · lp 2', 'tuple · price 20.00'],
];

const versionRows = [
  ['(0,1)', '712', '964', '10.00'],
  ['(0,2)', '964', '0', '20.00'],
];

const laneSteps = [
  ['BEGIN', 'SELECT price', '10.00'],
  ['BEGIN', 'SELECT price', '20.00'],
];

const horizonBars = [
  { tone: 'is-open', width: '100%', offset: '0' },
  { tone: '', width: '24%', offset: '30%' },
  { tone: '', width: '24%', offset: '58%' },
  { tone: 'is-dead', width: '100%', offset: '0' },
];

const sources = [
  ['Video', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q9jixKv4h2I', 'you won’t forget how postgres works after this'],
  ['PostgreSQL', 'https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/storage-page-layout.html', 'Database Page Layout'],
  ['PostgreSQL', 'https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/storage-hot.html', 'Heap-Only Tuples (HOT)'],
  ['PostgreSQL', 'https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/mvcc-intro.html', 'Concurrency Control: Introduction'],
  ['PostgreSQL', 'https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/transaction-iso.html', 'Transaction Isolation'],
  ['PostgreSQL', 'https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/routine-vacuuming.html', 'Routine Vacuuming'],
  ['PostgreSQL', 'https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/ddl-system-columns.html', 'System Columns'],
];
---

<Layout
  mainId="top"
  title={t.title}
  description={t.description}
  lang={lang}
  alternateHref={alternatePath}
  ogType="article"
  publishedTime="2026-08-26"
>
  <header class="sd-header db-header">
    <a class="brand" href="/system-design/#field-notes" aria-label={t.back}>
      <span class="brand-monogram" aria-hidden="true">MF</span>
      <span>Matías Fernández <em>/ System Design</em></span>
    </a>
    <div class="db-header-actions">
      <a href={alternatePath} aria-label={t.switchLabel}>{t.switchShort}</a>
      <span class="sd-header-label">{t.headerLabel}</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="top" tabindex="-1" class="db-page pg-page">
    <article>
      <header class="db-hero section-shell">
        <div class="db-breadcrumb-row">
          <p class="db-breadcrumb">
            <a href="/system-design/">{t.breadcrumb[0]}</a><span>/</span>
            <a href="/system-design/#field-notes">{t.breadcrumb[1]}</a><span>/</span><b>{t.breadcrumb[2]}</b>
          </p>
          <a class="db-language-link" href={alternatePath}>{t.switchLabel} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>

        <div class="db-hero-grid">
          <div class="db-hero-copy">
            <p class="db-kicker"><span></span>{t.kicker}</p>
            <h1>{t.heroA}<br /><em>{t.heroEm}</em></h1>
            <p>{t.lede}</p>
          </div>

          <figure class="pg-chain" aria-label={t.chainCaption[0]}>
            <figcaption><span>{t.chainCaption[0]}</span><b>{t.chainCaption[1]}</b></figcaption>
            <ol>
              {t.chain.map(([name, note], index) => (
                <li class={`chain-${index + 1}`}>
                  <span>0{index + 1}</span>
                  <div><strong>{name}</strong><small>{note}</small></div>
                  {index < t.chain.length - 1 && <b aria-hidden="true">↓</b>}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ol>
            <p><span>{t.chainFoot[0]}</span><i></i><span>{t.chainFoot[1]}</span></p>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <dl class="db-meta">
          {t.meta.map(([label, value]) => <div><dt>{label}</dt><dd>{value}</dd></div>)}
        </dl>
      </header>

      <aside class="db-thesis"><div class="section-shell"><span>{t.thesisLabel}</span><p>{t.thesis}</p></div></aside>

      <section class="db-section section-shell" id="pages">
        <div class="db-section-heading"><p>{t.s1Number}</p><div><h2>{t.s1Title[0]}<br /><em>{t.s1Title[1]}</em></h2><p>{t.s1Intro}</p></div></div>

        <div class="db-query-board">
          <div class="db-query-intro"><p>{t.boardLabel}</p><h3>{t.boardTitle}</h3><p>{t.boardCopy}</p></div>
          <ol>
            {queries.map((query, index) => (
              <li><span>0{index + 1} · {t.boardLabels[index]}</span><code>{query}</code></li>
            ))}
          </ol>
          <aside><span>{t.boardCalloutLabel}</span><p>{t.boardCallout}</p></aside>
        </div>

        <h3 class="db-subheading">{t.canvasTitle}</h3>
        <div class="db-canvas-grid">
          {t.canvas.map(([number, title, copy]) => <article><span>{number}</span><h4>{title}</h4><p>{copy}</p></article>)}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="db-section section-shell" id="page-layout">
        <div class="db-section-heading"><p>{t.s2Number}</p><div><h2>{t.s2Title[0]}<br /><em>{t.s2Title[1]}</em></h2><p>{t.s2Intro}</p></div></div>

        <figure class="pg-figure pg-anatomy">
          <figcaption><span>{t.anatomyCaption[0]}</span><b>{t.anatomyCaption[1]}</b></figcaption>
          <div class="pg-anatomy-row"><span>{t.anatomyLabels[0]}</span><p class="pg-band">{t.anatomyHeader}</p></div>
          <div class="pg-anatomy-row">
            <span>{t.anatomyLabels[1]}</span>
            <div class="pg-slots">{pointers.map((pointer) => <i>{pointer}</i>)}</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pg-anatomy-row"><span>{t.anatomyLabels[2]}</span><p class="pg-band">{t.anatomyFree}</p></div>
          <div class="pg-anatomy-row">
            <span>{t.anatomyLabels[3]}</span>
            <div class="pg-tuples">
              {t.anatomyTuples.map(([name, detail], index) => (
                <div class={index === 0 ? 'is-live' : ''}><b>{name}</b><span>{detail}</span></div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="pg-figure-foot"><span>{t.anatomyFootLabel}</span><p>{t.anatomyFoot}</p></div>
        </figure>

        <div class="db-index-cards">
          {t.pageCards.map(([number, title, copy]) => <article><span>{number}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></article>)}
        </div>

        <blockquote class="db-authority"><span>{t.authorityLabel}</span><p>{t.authority}</p></blockquote>
      </section>

      <section class="db-section pg-dark" id="heap"><div class="section-shell">
        <div class="db-section-heading light"><p>{t.s3Number}</p><div><h2>{t.s3Title[0]}<br /><em>{t.s3Title[1]}</em></h2><p>{t.s3Intro}</p></div></div>

        <figure class="pg-lookup">
          <figcaption><span>{t.lookupCaption[0]}</span><b>{t.lookupCaption[1]}</b></figcaption>
          <div class="pg-lookup-flow">
            {t.lookupPanels.map(([label, title, copy], index) => (
              <>
                <div class="pg-panel">
                  <span>{label}</span>
                  <h3>{title}</h3>
                  <div class="pg-nodes">
                    {lookupNodes[index].map((node, nodeIndex) => (
                      <i class={nodeIndex === lookupHits[index] ? 'is-hit' : ''}>{node}</i>
                    ))}
                  </div>
                  <p>{copy}</p>
                </div>
                {index < t.lookupPanels.length - 1 && <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>}
              </>
            ))}
          </div>
          <div class="pg-lookup-foot"><span>{t.lookupFootLabel}</span><p>{t.lookupFoot}</p></div>
        </figure>

        <aside class="pg-note"><span>{t.note3Label}</span><p>{t.note3}</p></aside>
      </div></section>

      <section class="db-section section-shell" id="mvcc">
        <div class="db-section-heading"><p>{t.s4Number}</p><div><h2>{t.s4Title[0]}<br /><em>{t.s4Title[1]}</em></h2><p>{t.s4Intro}</p></div></div>

        <figure class="pg-figure pg-versions">
          <figcaption><span>{t.versionsCaption[0]}</span><b>{t.versionsCaption[1]}</b></figcaption>
          <div class="pg-table-wrap">
            <table>
              <thead><tr>{t.versionsHead.map((heading) => <th scope="col">{heading}</th>)}</tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                {versionRows.map((row, index) => (
                  <tr class={index === 0 ? 'is-dead' : 'is-live'}>
                    <td><b>{row[0]}</b></td><td>{row[1]}</td><td>{row[2]}</td><td>{row[3]}</td>
                    <td>{t.versionStates[index]}</td>
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <div class="pg-figure-foot"><span>{t.versionsFootLabel}</span><p>{t.versionsFoot}</p></div>
        </figure>

        <div class="db-scale-cards">
          {t.opCards.map(([number, title, summary, cost], index) => (
            <article class={`scale-${index + 1}`}><span>{number}</span><h3>{title}</h3><strong>{summary}</strong><p>{cost}</p></article>
          ))}
        </div>

        <aside class="db-scale-callout"><span>{t.s4CalloutLabel}</span><p>{t.s4Callout}</p></aside>
      </section>

      <section class="db-section pg-dark" id="visibility"><div class="section-shell">
        <div class="db-section-heading light"><p>{t.s5Number}</p><div><h2>{t.s5Title[0]}<br /><em>{t.s5Title[1]}</em></h2><p>{t.s5Intro}</p></div></div>

        <figure class="pg-snapshot">
          <figcaption><span>{t.snapshotCaption[0]}</span><b>{t.snapshotCaption[1]}</b></figcaption>
          {t.lanes.map(([tag, title, note], index) => (
            <div class="pg-lane">
              <div><span>{tag}</span><strong>{title}</strong><small>{note}</small></div>
              <div class="pg-steps">
                {laneSteps[index].map((step, stepIndex) => (
                  <>
                    <i class={stepIndex === 2 ? 'is-visible' : ''}>{step}</i>
                    {stepIndex < 2 && <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>}
                  </>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
          <div class="pg-lookup-foot"><span>{t.snapshotFootLabel}</span><p>{t.snapshotFoot}</p></div>
        </figure>

        <aside class="pg-note"><span>{t.note5Label}</span><p>{t.note5}</p></aside>
      </div></section>

      <section class="db-section section-shell" id="hot">
        <div class="db-section-heading"><p>{t.s6Number}</p><div><h2>{t.s6Title[0]}<br /><em>{t.s6Title[1]}</em></h2><p>{t.s6Intro}</p></div></div>

        <figure class="db-index-figure pg-hot">
          {t.hotSides.map(([label, title, copy], index) => (
            <div>
              <span>{label}</span>
              <h3>{title}</h3>
              <div class="pg-heap">
                {t.hotRows[index].map(([name, detail], rowIndex) => (
                  <div class={rowIndex === 0 ? 'is-index' : rowIndex === 1 ? 'is-old' : 'is-new'}>
                    <b>{name}</b><span>{detail}</span>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
              <p>{copy}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
          <figcaption><span>{t.hotFootLabel}</span><p>{t.hotFoot}</p></figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="db-section section-shell" id="vacuum">
        <div class="db-section-heading"><p>{t.s7Number}</p><div><h2>{t.s7Title[0]}<br /><em>{t.s7Title[1]}</em></h2><p>{t.s7Intro}</p></div></div>

        <figure class="pg-figure pg-horizon">
          <figcaption><span>{t.horizonCaption[0]}</span><b>{t.horizonCaption[1]}</b></figcaption>
          <div class="pg-horizon-track">
            {t.horizonRows.map(([label, text], index) => (
              <div class="pg-horizon-row">
                <span>{label}</span>
                <p class={`pg-bar ${horizonBars[index].tone}`} style={`--w: ${horizonBars[index].width}; --x: ${horizonBars[index].offset};`}>{text}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
          <div class="pg-figure-foot"><span>{t.horizonFootLabel}</span><p>{t.horizonFoot}</p></div>
        </figure>

        <h3 class="db-subheading">{t.vacuumTitle}</h3>
        <div class="db-canvas-grid">
          {t.vacuumCards.map(([number, title, copy]) => <article><span>{number}</span><h4>{title}</h4><p>{copy}</p></article>)}
        </div>

        <aside class="pg-warning"><span>{t.warningLabel}</span><p>{t.warning}</p></aside>
      </section>

      <section class="db-section section-shell" id="practice">
        <div class="db-section-heading"><p>{t.s8Number}</p><div><h2>{t.s8Title[0]}<br /><em>{t.s8Title[1]}</em></h2><p>{t.s8Intro}</p></div></div>
        <ol class="db-method">{t.method.map(([number, title, copy]) => <li><span>{number}</span><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></div></li>)}</ol>
        <section class="db-checklist">
          <div><p>{t.checklistKicker}</p><h3>{t.checklistTitle}</h3></div>
          <ol>{t.checklist.map((item, index) => <li><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>{item}</li>)}</ol>
        </section>
      </section>

      <section class="db-conclusion"><div class="section-shell"><p class="db-kicker"><span></span>{t.conclusionKicker}</p><h2>{t.conclusionA}<br /><strong>{t.conclusionB}</strong></h2><p>{t.conclusionCopy}</p></div></section>

      <section class="db-sources section-shell">
        <div><p>{t.sourceNumber}</p><h2>{t.sourceTitle[0]}<br /><em>{t.sourceTitle[1]}</em></h2></div>
        <ol>{sources.map(([publisher, href, title], index) => <li><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><a href={href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><small>{publisher}</small><strong>{title}</strong><p>{t.sourceDescriptions[index]} ↗</p></a></li>)}</ol>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>

  <footer><a class="brand footer-brand" href="/system-design/#field-notes" aria-label={t.back}><span class="brand-monogram" aria-hidden="true">MF</span><span>Matías Fernández</span></a><p>{t.footer}</p><a href="#top">{t.top}</a></footer>
</Layout>
